                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "38ca89f1-5344-39e8-a430-dc0528f54ac5",
                        "entry_id": "8bab1cb9-c411-3c7e-9d35-a89ebdab80c7",
                        "glosses": [
                            "To enthrone."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "obsolete"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "fd611a56-de5a-4661-973a-450b591503e1",
                                "sense_id": "38ca89f1-5344-39e8-a430-dc0528f54ac5",
                                "text": "So then to conclude, though man bee Gods hand, and inſtrument, to inaugure, inthronize, and inueſt, yet is it God alone, that doth originally ordaine, inſtitute, and appoint."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "1a772b10-8d59-47e4-bb41-25b1db3790db",
                                "sense_id": "38ca89f1-5344-39e8-a430-dc0528f54ac5",
                                "text": "[T]hey cried out they muſt have a Muſulman Emperor; therefore they broke into a Dungeon, and brought out Muſtapha Oſman’s Unkle, whom he had clapt there at the beginning of the Tumult, and who had been King before, but was depos’d for his Simplicity, being a kind of Santon or holy Man, that is, ’twixt an Innocent and an Idiot: This Muſtapha they did re[-]inthronize and place in the Ottoman Empire."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "91946554-e9dc-4aef-abe1-fc3d45aff270",
                                "sense_id": "38ca89f1-5344-39e8-a430-dc0528f54ac5",
                                "text": "The which day in presens of us Connotaries publick, and witnesses underwritten, compeared a Reverende Father of God, Patricke Bishop of Aberdene, and presented to us Connotaries underwritten, within the Cathedrall Church of Olde Aberdene, at the pulpit of the same, the act of his Lordship's consecration and admission to the Bishopricke of Aberdene; requyring and commanding the Arch-Deane of the said Cathedrall Church to induce and inthronize the sayd Patrick, by himselfe, or his procurators, sufficientlie appoynted to that effect, in the said Bishopricke, at what tyme it should please his Lordship to requyre the same."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "63920c27-d731-4192-8ed0-99b94999eec7",
                                "sense_id": "38ca89f1-5344-39e8-a430-dc0528f54ac5",
                                "text": "I put it off all I can, becauſe I wold avoyde any further Jorney then to Paris, hoping that the King will now be thinking of his return thither to inthronize his new Queen; whereof I wold have been very glad to have underſtood ſome certainty from you, and do yet deſire to know as ſoon as may be, what is the King's purpoſe in it; that at my coming in Paris, I may be able to reſolve what to do."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "7e893a9f-9471-4586-a1d7-16c66c0be287",
                                "sense_id": "38ca89f1-5344-39e8-a430-dc0528f54ac5",
                                "text": "After wich [the] King ascendit the stage, attendit by diuers of the pryme officers and nobilitie, the queir singing, \"Te Deum laudamus;\" wich being endit, the Archbischope did inthronize the King, [...]"
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
